<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bhavavarman I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">6th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bhavavarman I was a king of Chenla in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambodia">Cambodia</a> in the second half of the 6th century. With his relative <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahendravarman-chenla">Chitrasena</a>, the future Mahendravarman, he attacked Funan, the older kingdom of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mekong-river">Mekong</a> delta, and Chenla displaced it as the main power of the region. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a> inscriptions record his religious foundations, and he is regarded as one of the first rulers of a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-empire">Khmer</a> state.</p></div>
